-- title:
--   Integrality of y x^{-m} over the inverted base
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a nontrivial commutative ring, $K$ a field and $f : R \to K$ a ring homomorphism. Let $P \in R[X][Y]$ be a bivariate polynomial over $R$, monic as a polynomial in the outer variable $Y$, of degree $n = P.\mathrm{natDegree}$, and let $m$ be a natural number such that for every $i < n$ the coefficient $P_i \in R[X]$ of $Y^i$ satisfies $\deg P_i \le m(n-i)$. Let $x \in K$ be nonzero and $y \in K$, and suppose $y$ is a root of the one-variable polynomial over $K$ obtained from $P$ by applying to its coefficients the evaluation homomorphism $R[X] \to K$ determined by $f$ and $x$; that is, $P.\mathrm{eval}_2(\mathrm{eval}_2\mathrm{RingHom}\,f\,x)\,y = 0$. The assertion is that there exists $Q \in R[X][Y]$ which is monic in $Y$, has the same $Y$-degree $n$ as $P$, and satisfies $Q.\mathrm{eval}_2(\mathrm{eval}_2\mathrm{RingHom}\,f\,x^{-1})\,(y\,x^{-m}) = 0$. Thus $y\,x^{-m}$ is integral over the subring of $K$ generated by $f(R)$ together with $x^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the reciprocal-polynomial (degree-reflection) integrality step: a bound $\deg P_i \le m(n-i)$ on the coefficients of a monic equation for $y$ over $f(R)[x]$ converts into a monic equation of the same degree for $y/x^{m}$ over $f(R)[x^{-1}]$. It is used in the construction of fibre models on the chart at infinity of the modular curve in characteristic $p$, and in the identification of elements annihilated there.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_CharPModel_exists_monic_eval2_inv_mul_inv_pow_eq_zero.lean

